      {
        "t": 97.21,
        "who": "Centi",
        "text": "Exactly. Now. Your father's shelves. Two parallel lines, and one diagonal brace cutting across them. That diagonal is called a transversal. It sounds fancy. It's a stick."
      },
      {
        "t": 108.35,
        "who": "Centi",
        "text": "Alternate angles are equal. They make a Z shape. Corresponding angles are equal. They make an F shape. Co interior angles sit inside, on the same side, in a C shape. Those add up to one hundred and eighty."
      },
      {
        "t": 121.67,
        "who": "Tara",
        "text": "So if the top angle is seventy, the Z angle at the bottom is also seventy, and the C angle next to it is one hundred and ten."
      },
      {
        "t": 130.01,
        "who": "Centi",
        "text": "And if your father measures seventy at the top and sixty five at the bottom, the shelves aren't parallel. Which is why the books are now on the floor. Doing their own reading."
      },
      {
        "t": 141.92,
        "who": "Dad",
        "text": "The shelf is parallel. The floor isn't. I've written to the H D B."
      },
      {
        "t": 146.58,
        "who": "Dad",
        "text": "They have not replied. Which I take as agreement."
      }
